<h1>4. Feeding for Weight and FCR</h1>
<p class="lead">Feed is 70-75% of your broiler cost. Every point of FCR you improve is direct profit.</p>
<div class="meta"><strong>Module 4 of 6</strong> · Broiler Farming for Profit · quiz at the end</div>
<h2>Lesson 4.1 - The three phases</h2>
<table>
<tr><th>Feed</th><th>Weeks</th><th>Protein</th><th>Cost/50 kg</th></tr>
<tr><td>Broiler starter</td><td>0-3</td><td>22-23%</td><td>30-42</td></tr>
<tr><td>Broiler grower</td><td>3-5</td><td>19-21%</td><td>28-38</td></tr>
<tr><td>Broiler finisher</td><td>5-7</td><td>18-20%</td><td>28-36</td></tr>
</table>
<p>Never switch abruptly. Mix old and new feed for 3 days at each change.</p>
<h2>Lesson 4.2 - FCR and cost per kg</h2>
<p>FCR = kg feed consumed / kg live weight gained.</p>
<table>
<tr><th>FCR</th><th>Verdict</th><th>Feed cost/kg live at 0.55/kg</th></tr>
<tr><td>1.6-1.8</td><td>Excellent</td><td>0.88-0.99</td></tr>
<tr><td>1.8-2.0</td><td>Good</td><td>0.99-1.10</td></tr>
<tr><td>2.0-2.2</td><td>Acceptable</td><td>1.10-1.21</td></tr>
<tr><td>2.2-2.5</td><td>Poor</td><td>1.21-1.38</td></tr>
<tr><td>Above 2.5</td><td>Not profitable</td><td>Above 1.38</td></tr>
</table>
<div class="callout"><strong>The FCR rule:</strong> Cutting FCR from 2.2 to 1.9 saves 0.17 per kg live weight. On 200 birds x 2 kg that is 68 per batch.</div>
<h2>Lesson 4.3 - Reducing feed waste</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>Fill feeders to 2/3, not full.</strong> Birds scatter feed when overfilled.</li>
<li><strong>Raise feeder lip as birds grow.</strong> Level with the back.</li>
<li><strong>Use nipple drinkers.</strong> Wet feed is thrown away.</li>
<li><strong>Store feed sealed, off the ground, dry.</strong></li>
<li><strong>Feed at the same time daily.</strong></li>
<li><strong>Do not overstock.</strong> Crowded birds scratch feed onto litter.</li>
</ul>
<h2>Lesson 4.4 - Home-mixing</h2>
<table>
<tr><th>Ingredient</th><th>Starter %</th><th>Grower %</th><th>Finisher %</th></tr>
<tr><td>Maize (ground)</td><td>55</td><td>60</td><td>65</td></tr>
<tr><td>Soya meal</td><td>25</td><td>20</td><td>17</td></tr>
<tr><td>Fish meal</td><td>5</td><td>4</td><td>3</td></tr>
<tr><td>Wheat bran</td><td>8</td><td>9</td><td>8</td></tr>
<tr><td>Limestone</td><td>1</td><td>1</td><td>1</td></tr>
<tr><td>DCP</td><td>2</td><td>2</td><td>2</td></tr>
<tr><td>Salt</td><td>0.3</td><td>0.3</td><td>0.3</td></tr>
<tr><td>Premix</td><td>0.25</td><td>0.25</td><td>0.25</td></tr>
</table>
<div class="warn"><strong>Home-mixing requires accurate scales.</strong> Buy a 20 USD scale before you home-mix. If you can't weigh, buy commercial feed.</div>
<div class="good"><strong>Practical exercise 4.1:</strong> Weigh feed for one week. Weigh 10 random birds at week 4 and 6. Calculate FCR.</div>
